@@@ recovery-readme
type: text_file
title: RECOVERY NOTES — read me first
author: archivist
date: 2026-10-27T09:00:00-07:00
path: /RECOVERY_NOTES.txt
role: critical
---
RECOVERY NOTES
==============
Source media, bought together as one lot at a Seattle hardware
surplus auction, 2026:

  1. One HP DAT24 tape, hand-labelled "BEACON FULL 17-OCT-99".
     Readable to about 38% of its length. Everything after that
     point is unreadable.
  2. One 1U rack server from a colocation facility, with a 9 GB
     disk. It holds a partial restore of the tape above, plus a
     few files written to it in October 1999.

What follows is everything that could be read from both.
File dates are the dates inside the files, not recovery dates.
Where bytes were unreadable, they are shown as ▒.
Where a page links to something that was not recovered, the link
is kept and marked missing. Missing does not mean deleted. It
means we don't have it. Those are different things.

The Lighthouse Network was a small online community of radio
listeners on the Oregon and Washington coast, 1997-1999. It went
offline in October 1999. Nobody wrote down why.

